As promised after our meeting, here's an overview of Normain's role/permission model and how SharePoint access works — so you can plan your access provisioning.

**How the roles work:**

* **Org owner** and **Org manager** are organization-level administrative roles. They are optional and held only by selected users — most users have neither, and a user can hold at most one.

* For every team they belong to, a user has one **team-level** role — either **Team owner** or **Team member**.

* So a typical user has no org-level role and is simply a Team owner or Team member in their teams; administrators additionally hold Org owner or Org manager.

